==English==
{{wikipedia|Cyrillic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla|en}} languages, especially using the Cyrillic script, compare Russian {{l|ru|а́збука}} (also Belarusian, Bulgarian, Macedonian, Serbo-Croatian, Ukrainian), from the first {{etyl|cu|en}} letter names [[аз]] (az) and [[буки]] (búki) (compare Ancient Greek {{l|grc|ἀλφάβητος}} = {{m|grc|ἄλφα|sc=polytonic}} + {{m|grc|βῆτα|sc=polytonic}} or Persian {{l|fa|الف|tr=alef}} + {{l|fa|باء|tr=bâ}}), from {{etyl|sla-pro|en}} {{m|sla-pro|*(j)azъ}}, {{m|sla-pro|*buky}}.

